    {
      "id": "sol.amc-12a-2002-p1.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "Factoring out \\(2x+3\\) gives \\((2x+3)\\big[(x-4)+(x-6)\\big]\\) \\(= (2x+3)(2x-10)\\) \\(= 0.\\)\n\nThe roots are \\(-\\dfrac{3}{2}\\) and \\(5,\\) whose sum is \\(-\\dfrac{3}{2} + 5 = \\dfrac{7}{2}.\\)\n\nThus, the correct answer is A.",
      "hints": [
        "Both terms share the factor \\(2x+3\\)",
        "The equation becomes \\((2x+3)(2x-10)=0\\)"
      ],
      "images": []
    }
